everybody loves in jokes and Hollywood  filmmakers are no exception tracking  down their carefully concealed Easter  eggs has become a full-time hobby for  some fans but even the most practiced I  occasionally misses something here's a  look at some well hidden Easter eggs  that flew by even the biggest movie fans  the departed it only makes sense that a  film scholar like Martin Scorsese would  pay homage to those who came before him  with some well-placed Easter eggs and he  did just that in the 2006 film The  Departed which used hidden exits on  screen to signal which characters were  going to die just like in the 1932  gangland classic Scarface even more  subtle the only straight shooter in the  film Dignam usually appears with a  straight line behind his head leave it  to Scorsese to hide an easter egg within  an easter egg Toy Story you wouldn't  expect the family-friendly classic Toy  Story to be linked with the decidedly  non family-friendly horror opus The  Shining but there are actually a number  of Easter eggs in the Toy Story  franchise referencing Stanley Kubrick's  masterpiece the first and most subtle of  them all the carpet in since house of  horrors is almost identical to the  carpet in the Shining's iconic Hotel  will never look at Woody's escape quite  the same way again Wes Craven and Sam  Raimi you really can't talk about the  history of horror movies over the last  few decades without referencing director  Sam Raimi and Wes Craven which is  fitting because the two also referenced  each other in nearly all of their  projects it began in Raimi's 1981 film  The Evil Dead which included a poster of  Cravens classic The Hills Have Eyes  Kraven answered by having a character in  1984 a Nightmare on Elm Street watched  the Evil Dead Raimi upped the ante by  placing Freddy's iconic glove in a  couple of scenes in 1987's Evil Dead 2  and the friendly rivalry even continued  into the 90s with Cravens screen showing  a group of teenagers choosing not to  watch Evil Dead that spelled out the end  of their on-screen back and forth until  after Cravens death in 2015 when Raimi  paid homage in season 2 of ash vs. Evil  Dead by once again including a poster  The Hills Have Eyes die hard with a  vengeance in the 1995 blockbuster die  hard with a vengeance John McClane is  past  what he's been doing since the events of  die hard - he responds that he's been  smoking cigarettes and watching Captain  Kangaroo  that's a nod to the Statler Brothers  song flowers on the wall which his  character in 1994's pulp fiction is  listening to during a particularly  memorable scene and the easter-egg had  extra significance because die hard with  a vengeance also featured Pulp Fiction  star samuel l.jackson neato  Zootopia you might not think frozen and  Zootopia have much in common other than  both being huge disney mega hits but  midway through Zootopia Judy and Nick  interrogate a suspect who is very  familiar to fans of frozen what were you  gonna do at those night howlers weselton  it's weaselton the character is voiced  by alan tudyk who not coincidentally  played a very similar character in  frozen the duke of weaseltown hiring the  same voice actor to set up an easter egg  now that's going above and beyond Back  to the Future in the classic Bullwinkle  segment pee buddies improbable history a  boy named Sherman travels through time  learning lessons from his mentor the  super intelligent dog Peabody if that  sounds like the premise of Back to the  Future where a boy named Marty travels  through time and learns lessons from his  mentor dr. ow don't worry because those  parallels weren't lost on the folks  making Back to the Future when Marty  arrives in the past he crashes into a  barn and encounters a wide-eyed kid who  thinks Marty is an alien that boy's name  Sherman Peabody well played fight club  David Fincher has earned a reputation as  a meticulous director over the years  with stories of actors having to suffer  through hundreds of tapes to find the  exact one he wants but even for Fincher  his keen attention to detail and Fight  Club takes the cake or the coffee he  claims to have included a Starbucks cup  somewhere in every single scene  when deep space exploration ramps up  it'll be the corporations that name  everything planet Starbucks there are  tons of subtle hints that point to the  movies big Tyler Durden plot twist but  this might be the only ongoing Easter  Egg that took a ridiculous amount of  planning to offer an uncanny commentary  on the proliferation of brand awareness  and ownership hidden in a movie that  openly denounces the corporate ownership  of human lives thanks for watching click  the looper icon to subscribe to our  YouTube channel plus check out all this  cool stuff we know you'll love to  [Applause]
 

